/*
 * Declares TypeTable, the types of the module a pass can add to.
 *
 * A YIL type is named by its uid, by the backend that caches the tree it builds
 * of it as much as by the files the module is exported to. A pass building a
 * value of a type the expander never produced has therefore to give it a uid no
 * other type of the module holds, and to hand it to the export with the others.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::lint::optimizer::typetable
 * @File: ymirc/lint/optimizer/typetable.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-09-24
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
